* stmono2.scheme
* dash translation of Stata's stmono2 graph scheme.
*
* Source Stata scheme file : /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-stmono2.scheme
*                            (#include chain resolved: s2color -> s2mono -> stmono2)
* Stata version            : StataNow 19.5 (MP), born 12 Aug 2026
* Extracted (UTC)          : 2026-09-18T18:58:04Z
* Translated (local date)  : 2026-09-18
*
* DERIVATION.  Every value below is copied from the "stmono2" entry of
*   test/fixtures/scheme_truth.json, which scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py
*   resolved from Stata's own scheme-*.scheme and style/*.style files.  This
*   file is NOT hand-tuned and NOT eyeballed from a rendered graph.  Re-run the
*   extractor after a Stata upgrade to confirm it is still true; the version and
*   date above record when it last was.
*
* COLOURS ARE RESOLVED HEX ON PURPOSE.  dash's OptionTranslator._COLOR_MAP
*   carries only a subset of Stata's colour names, and SchemeParser._color()
*   silently substitutes its "#000000" default for a token it cannot translate.
*   Writing #rrggbb keeps this file self-contained and immune to that failure.
*
* Property categories used by dash SchemeParser:
*   color, symbol, linepattern, linewidth, intensity, gsize, graphsize,
*   symbolsize, clockdir, numstyle
*
* The fixture reports no unresolvable properties for stmono2 ("unresolvable":
*   []) and no null (Stata colour "none") values, so nothing is omitted here for
*   want of ground truth.  Every directive below is one the fixture's own
*   "sources" map names; none is invented.  Two of them - "yesno
*   draw_major_hgrid" and "yesno draw_major_grid" - are real Stata directives
*   that SchemeParser._init_properties() does not yet read; they are recorded
*   anyway because the scheme file is the only place they can come from, and
*   test_scheme_fidelity.py checks them out of SchemeParser._props.  They are
*   inert until dash learns to consume them.

label "stmono2"

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Background and region colors
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color background      #ffffff
color plotregion      #ffffff
color legend          #ffffff
color legend_line     #ffffff
color major_grid      #e8e8e8
color minor_grid      #505050
color heading         #000000
color axisline        #000000

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Per-plot color cycle (p1-p15)
* Source directives: color p1 .. color p15
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color p1      #606060
color p2      #a0a0a0
color p3      #808080
color p4      #404040
color p5      #000000
color p6      #c0c0c0
color p7      #202020
color p8      #707070
color p9      #909090
color p10     #b0b0b0
color p11     #d0d0d0
color p12     #505050
color p13     #303030
color p14     #c0c0c0
color p15     #505050

* Per-plot line color (for line/connected plots).
* stmono2 sets no per-index line colour: all 15 resolve through the "color
* pline" stub, which is black.  Written out per index because dash reads
* "color p#line" only.
color p1line   #000000
color p2line   #000000
color p3line   #000000
color p4line   #000000
color p5line   #000000
color p6line   #000000
color p7line   #000000
color p8line   #000000
color p9line   #000000
color p10line  #000000
color p11line  #000000
color p12line  #000000
color p13line  #000000
color p14line  #000000
color p15line  #000000

* Per-plot bar/area fill color.  No "color p#bar" in stmono2; each entry
* resolves through the p# fallback to the plot colour above.
color p1bar    #606060
color p2bar    #a0a0a0
color p3bar    #808080
color p4bar    #404040
color p5bar    #000000
color p6bar    #c0c0c0
color p7bar    #202020
color p8bar    #707070
color p9bar    #909090
color p10bar   #b0b0b0
color p11bar   #d0d0d0
color p12bar   #505050
color p13bar   #303030
color p14bar   #c0c0c0
color p15bar   #505050

* Per-plot marker fill color (scatter).  Same fallback as the bar colours.
color p1mark   #606060
color p2mark   #a0a0a0
color p3mark   #808080
color p4mark   #404040
color p5mark   #000000
color p6mark   #c0c0c0
color p7mark   #202020
color p8mark   #707070
color p9mark   #909090
color p10mark  #b0b0b0
color p11mark  #d0d0d0
color p12mark  #505050
color p13mark  #303030
color p14mark  #c0c0c0
color p15mark  #505050

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Marker symbol cycle
* Stata style names, kept verbatim.  dash's translate_msymbol() does not yet
* know smdiamond or smtriangle and falls back to a circle for those two; that
* is a dash_render limitation, not a mistranslation of the scheme.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbol p1     circle
symbol p2     diamond
symbol p3     square
symbol p4     triangle
symbol p5     x
symbol p6     plus
symbol p7     circle_hollow
symbol p8     diamond_hollow
symbol p9     square_hollow
symbol p10    triangle_hollow
symbol p11    smcircle
symbol p12    smdiamond
symbol p13    smsquare
symbol p14    smtriangle
symbol p15    smx

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line patterns for line/connected plots.
* stmono2 sets only the bare "linepattern p" default (solid); it distinguishes
* series by grey value, not by dash pattern.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linepattern p1line   solid
linepattern p2line   solid
linepattern p3line   solid
linepattern p4line   solid
linepattern p5line   solid
linepattern p6line   solid
linepattern p7line   solid
linepattern p8line   solid
linepattern p9line   solid
linepattern p10line  solid
linepattern p11line  solid
linepattern p12line  solid
linepattern p13line  solid
linepattern p14line  solid
linepattern p15line  solid

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line widths (Stata linewidth style names)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linewidth p           medium
linewidth major_grid  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Fill intensities
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
intensity p        inten80
intensity bar      full
* No Stata base scheme sets "intensity area"; stmono2 resolves it through the
* bare intensity class default, which is full.
intensity area     full

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Font sizes (Stata gsize keywords)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gsize text          medium
gsize heading       large
gsize axis_title    medsmall
gsize tick_label    medsmall
gsize note          small

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Graph dimensions, in inches
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphsize x  7.5
graphsize y  4.5

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Grid switches.  Recorded from the fixture; dash does not read them yet.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
yesno draw_major_hgrid  yes
yesno draw_major_grid   no

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Marker size and legend placement
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbolsize p             small
clockdir legend_position 3
numstyle legend_cols     1
